 for  the nfl walter payton man of the year  award vincent jackson arrived in tampa  bay in 2012.  each of the four seasons after that that  he was with the team 13 14 15 16 he was  the nominee think of how quickly you  establish your presence from a  charitable standpoint  first year there yeah it's your first  year there you're not gonna you're not  gonna do so much your first year there  that you're the walter payton nfl man of  the year nominee but each of the next  four  that was the individual who received  that designation from the buccaneers  organization and the buccaneers  issued a statement yesterday as well  regarding the passing of vincent jackson  and there was a flood of tweets from  various teammates executives etc who had  been with vincent jackson it really  wasn't all that long ago he's remember  this buccaneers team i remember mike  evans was drafted in 2014  between evans and jackson one of the top  receiving duos in the nfl shereen right  out of the gates  it was and you saw you know mike evans  tweet and i honestly for a second forgot  that they had played together because it  doesn't seem like mike evans is that far  into his career  and then you start going back you're  like boy you know evans has played for a  while i played i mean he didn't  officially retire till 2018. it was a  couple years before that they last  played but you know this is a guy who  you truly remember of how good he was on  the field i go back mike to the 2007  playoffs when he was with the chargers  that was the chargers best chance with  philip rivers to go to the super bowl  and it's unfortunate that ladainian  thomason got hurt in the postseason but  vincent jackson and those three playoff  games that year he carried them more  than than the banged up lt did he hit  114 yards and a touchdown in the first  playoff game against tennessee the next  week against indianapolis seven catches  for 93 yards and a touchdown they came  back he kept him in the game against new  england then if the afc championship  game he had six catches for 93 yards and  and you have that memory of lt standing  over there on the sidelines injured with  the park on and the hoodie over his head  and vincent jackson was doing everything  he could to try to make up for the loss  of lt and we just was outstanding in  that postseason and i i do remember that  run i covered a couple of those games  and vincent jackson was incredible that  year in that playoff run  and you think back to 2014 what they had  at the skill position specifically  receiver in tight end the buccaneers had  mike evans first round pick six foot  five vincent jackson six foot five tight  end austin safari and jenkins who never  really worked out but there was a ton of  promise there six foot five and the  quarterback mike lennon was six foot  seven they had some very tall guys in  that window of time now obviously jameis  winston came along in 2015 as a first  overall pick in the draft but i i  remember now and and you know the years  go by so quickly with the nfl and every  team seems to have a completely  different makeup year in and year out  but  it kind of comes back to you as you  remember it and think through it that  they they had those three really big  targets going into 2014 and vincent  jackson still had plenty of gas in the  tank still and and was a great mentor  for a guy like a mike evans and it just  wasn't that long ago  that jackson was playing and playing at  a high level in the nfl and we extend  our condolences obviously to the family  friends teammates it it just it just is  another tragedy in the broader nfl  community  and uh there's tragedies all around us  that it just everywhere you turn whether  it's nfl or beyond the nfl and we're  just trying to get through life one day  at a time as we we await the broader  cloud of  of the pandemic to go away it just it  just has just been  a strange time as strange a time as i  can ever remember and and situations  like 